      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the values of \\( x \\) that satisfy the equation \\(\\sqrt[3]{x} + \\sqrt[3]{20 - x} = 2\\), we start by letting \\( \\sqrt[3]{x} = a \\) and \\( \\sqrt[3]{20 - x} = b \\). This gives us the system of equations:\n\n\\[ a + b = 2 \\]\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = 20 - x \\]\n\nWe know the identity for the sum of cubes:\n\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = (a + b)(a^2 - ab + b^2) \\]\n\nSubstituting \\( a + b = 2 \\) into the identity, we get:\n\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = 2(a^2 - ab + b^2) \\]\n\nWe also know that:\n\n\\[ a^2 + b^2 = (a + b)^2 - 2ab = 2^2 - 2ab = 4 - 2ab \\]\n\nSo, we have:\n\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = 2(4 - 2ab - ab) = 2(4 - 3ab) = 8 - 6ab \\]\n\nFrom the second equation \\( a^3 + b^3 = 20 - x \\), we get:\n\n\\[ 8 - 6ab = 20 - x \\]\n\\[ x = 6ab - 12 \\]\n\nNow, we need to find the values of \\( a \\) and \\( b \\). Since \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are real numbers, we can use the fact that \\( a + b = 2 \\). Let's assume \\( a = 1 + \\sqrt{3} \\) and \\( b = 1 - \\sqrt{3} \\). Then:\n\n\\[ a^2 - ab + b^2 = (1 + \\sqrt{3})^2 - (1 + \\sqrt{3})(1 - \\sqrt{3}) + (1 - \\sqrt{3})^2 \\]\n\\[ = 1 + 2\\sqrt{3} + 3 - 1 + 3 + 1 - 2\\sqrt{3} + 3 = 10 \\]\n\nSo, \\( ab = (1 + \\sqrt{3})(1 - \\sqrt{3}) = 1 - 3 = -2 \\). Then:\n\n\\[ x = 6ab - 12 = 6(-2) - 12 = -12 - 12 = -24 \\]\n\nHowever, we made an error in the assumption. Let's try \\( a = 1 - \\sqrt{3} \\) and \\( b = 1 + \\sqrt{3} \\):\n\n\\[ a^2 - ab + b^2 = (1 - \\sqrt{3})^2 - (1 - \\sqrt{3})(1 + \\sqrt{3}) + (1 + \\sqrt{3})^2 \\]\n\\[ = 1 - 2\\sqrt{3} + 3 - 1 - 3 + 1 + 2\\sqrt{3} + 3 = 4 \\]\n\nSo, \\( ab = (-1)(1) = -1 \\). Then:\n\n\\[ x = 6ab - 12 = 6(-1) - 12 = -6 - 12 = -18 \\]\n\nThis is also incorrect. Let's try \\( a = 2 \\) and \\( b = 0 \\):\n\n\\[ a + b = 2 \\]\n\\[ a^3 + b^3 = 20 - x \\]\n\\[ 2^3 + 0^3 = 20 - x \\]\n\\[ 8 = 20 - x \\]\n\\[ x = 12 \\]\n\nSo, the smaller value of \\( x \\) is 6. We need to express this in the form \\( p - \\sqrt{q} \\). Since \\( 6 \\) is already in the form, \\( p = 6 \\) and \\( q = 0 \\). Therefore, \\( p + q = 6 + 0 = 6 \\).\n\nThe final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{6}\n\\]",
